  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida has $180M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.4% year over year. The state saw 1,077 awards with an average award size of $167K. Year-over-year totals show a sharp drop from prior full fiscal years: FY22 had $26.6B, FY23 had $29B, FY24 had $31.3B, FY25 had $32.4B, and FY26 had $32.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far with $93.8M obligated, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $58.7M and the Department of Homeland Security with $22M. BLUE ORIGIN, LLC is the top vendor with $46.1M in obligations, followed by METROIBR JV LLC with $22.7M and BLUE CORD DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION, LLC with $13M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest industry by obligation with $46.1M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $26M and Custom Computer Programming Services with $23.2M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year in Florida federal contracting?",
        "body": "Florida obligations fell 99.4% year over year. The state recorded $180M in FY2027 to date after full-year totals of $32.1B in FY26 and $32.4B in FY25. The count of awards in FY2027 to date is 1,077 with an average award size of $167K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buying agencies and vendors in Florida right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency with $93.8M in obligations. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $58.7M and the Department of Homeland Security with $22M. BLUE ORIGIN, LLC is the top vendor with $46.1M, followed by METROIBR JV LLC with $22.7M and BLUE CORD DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION, LLC with $13M."
      }
    ]
  },
